  },
  "question": {
    "text": "The number of matrices of order <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, whose entries are either <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>&nbsp;and the sum of all the entries is a prime number, is _______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "282",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Let the matrix be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>a</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>b</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>c</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>d</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>e</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>f</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>g</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>h</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>i</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced></math></p><p>Since the elements can be either of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>or</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, so</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>e</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>7</mn></math></p><p>For sum as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>, the number of cases will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn></math></p><p>For sum as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>, the number of cases will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>!</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>84</mn></math></p><p>For sum as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>, the number of cases will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>!</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>126</mn></math></p><p>For sum as&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math>, the number of cases will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>!</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>!</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn></math></p><p>Total required matrix will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>282</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
}